.TH DRAGONGL-SERVER 1 "2026-11-08" "DragonGL 2026.11.08.09" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl-server \- Dragon GL server launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl-server
.RB [ \-\-password\-file
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-dm\-password\-file
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-P | \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-D | \-\-data\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-S | \-\-state\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl-server
starts the Dragon GL game server
.BR dragongl_server (1).
It runs the binary installed next to it, or
.I build/dragongl_server
in a development tree. In a development tree it first changes to the
project root (where
.I data/
lives) and, unless a state directory is given, keeps the server state in
the git-ignored
.I state/
directory there.
.PP
Before starting the server it prints diagnostic information about the host
(operating system, uptime and load, memory, disk space, network
interfaces). The block includes the machine's IP addresses: set
.B DIAGNOSTICS=0
to skip it.
.PP
Passwords are never accepted on the command line, where every local user
can read them with
.BR ps (1).
The server access password comes from
.BR \-\-password\-file ,
from
.BR DRAGONGL_SERVER_PASSWORD ,
or, when the launcher runs on a terminal, from a prompt that also asks for
the optional Dungeon Master password. The passwords reach the server
through its environment, which the server wipes at start-up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " file"
Read the server access password from the first line of
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-\-dm\-password\-file " file"
Read the Dungeon Master password from the first line of
.IR file .
Without a DM password the
.B dm
account is disabled.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-port " \fIport\fR"
TCP port to listen on (default 8080).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-data\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
Data directory (see
.BR dragongl_server (1)).
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-state\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
State directory: world, NPCs, characters, logs (see
.BR dragongl_server (1)).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_SERVER_PASSWORD
Server access password, used when no
.B \-\-password\-file
is given.
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_DM_PASSWORD
Dungeon Master password (optional).
.TP
.B DIAGNOSTICS
Set to 0 to skip the host diagnostics block.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start interactively (the launcher asks for the passwords):
.PP
.RS
.B dragongl-server
.RE
.PP
Start from password files on another port:
.PP
.RS
.B chmod 600 server.pw dm.pw
.br
.B dragongl-server \-\-password\-file server.pw \-\-dm\-password\-file dm.pw \-\-port 9000
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_server (1),
.BR dragongl-client (1),
.BR dragongl-reset-world (1)
